iel","also":"","summary":"The chief of the Kohathites at the time when the ark was brought up to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 15:5, 11).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,11]},{"id":"merari_2004","name":"Merari","also":"","summary":"Sad; bitter, the youngest son of Levi, born before the descent of Jacob into Egypt, and one of the seventy who accompanied him thither (Gen. 46:11; Ex. 6:16).","verses":38,"father":"Levi","mother":"","v":[6,17]},{"id":"asaiah_328","name":"Asaiah","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,11]},{"id":"gershon_1305","name":"Gershon","also":"Gershom","summary":"Ger’shom expulsion, the eldest of Levi’s three sons (Gen. 46:11; Ex. 6:16).","verses":25,"father":"Levi","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"joel_1654","name":"Joel","also":"","summary":"A Levite of the family of Gershom (1 Chr. 15:7, 11).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7,11]},{"id":"elizaphan_1189","name":"Elizaphan","also":"Elzaphan","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"Uzziel","mother":"","v":[8]},{"id":"shemaiah_2625","name":"Shemaiah","also":"","summary":"A Levite in the time of David, who with 200 of his brethren took part in the bringing up of the ark from Obed-edom to Hebron (1 Chr. 15:8).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[8,11]},{"id":"hebron_1475","name":"Hebron","also":"","summary":"The third son of Kohath the Levite (Ex. 6:18; 1 Chr. 6:2, 18).","verses":8,"father":"Kohath","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"eliel_1110","name":"Eliel","also":"","summary":"Son of Hebron.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9,11]},{"id":"uzziel_2929","name":"Uzziel","also":"","summary":"One of the sons of Kohath, and uncle of Aaron (Ex. 6:18; Lev. 10:4).","verses":11,"father":"Kohath","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"amminadab_229","name":"Amminadab","also":"","summary":"Chief of the 112 descendants of Uzziel the Levite (1 Chr. 15:10, 11).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10,11]},{"id":"zadok_2973","name":"Zadok","also":"","summary":"A son of Ahitub, of the line of Eleazer (2 Sam. 8:17; 1 Chr. 24:3), high priest in the time of David (2 Sam. 20:25) and Solomon (1 Kings 4:4).","verses":40,"father":"Ahitub","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"abiathar_20","name":"Abiathar","also":"","summary":"Father of abundance, or my father excels, the son of Ahimelech the high priest. He was the tenth high priest, and the fourth in descent from Eli.","verses":29,"father":"Ahimelech","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[15]},{"id":"asaph_330","name":"Asaph","also":"","summary":"A Levite; one of the leaders of David’s choir (1 Chr. 6:39). Psalms 50 and 73-83 inclusive are attributed to him. He is mentioned along with David as skilled in music, and a “seer” (2 Chr. 29:30).","verses":32,"father":"Berechiah","mother":"","v":[17,19]},{"id":"jeduthun_1224","name":"Jeduthun","also":"Ethan","summary":"A Levite of the family of Merari, one of the leaders of the temple music (1 Chr. 6:44; 15:17, 19). He was probably the same as Jeduthun.","verses":13,"father":"Kishi","mother":"","v":[17,19]},{"id":"heman_1490","name":"Heman","also":"","summary":"Grandson of Samuel (1 Chr. 6:33; 15:17), to whom the 88th Psalm probably was inscribed.","verses":12,"father":"Joel","mother":"","v":[17,19]},{"id":"joel_1647","name":"Joel","also":"Vashni","summary":"The oldest of Samuel’s two sons appointed by him as judges in Beersheba (1 Sam. 8:2).","verses":4,"father":"Samuel","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"berechiah_469","name":"Berechiah","also":"Berachiah","summary":"Son of Shimea, and father of Asaph the musician (1 Chr. 6:39; 15:17).","verses":3,"father":"Shimea","mother":"","v":[17,23]},{"id":"kishi_1788","name":"Kishi","also":"Kushaiah","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Abdi","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"zechariah_3004","name":"Zechariah","also":"","summary":"A Levite who assisted at the bringing up of the ark from the house of Obededom (1 Chr. 15:20-24).","verses":7,"father":"Meshelemiah","mother":"","v":[18,20,24]},{"id":"benaiah_442","name":"Benaiah","also":"","summary":"A musical Levite (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20,24]},{"id":"mattithiah_1974","name":"Mattithiah","also":"","summary":"One of the sons of Jeduthun (1 Chr. 25:3, 21).","verses":5,"father":"Jeduthun","mother":"","v":[18,21]},{"id":"jeiel_827","name":"Jeiel","also":"Jehiah","summary":"One of the Levites who took part in praising God on the removal of the ark to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 16:5).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,21,24]},{"id":"eliab_1077","name":"Eliab","also":"","summary":"Lyre player.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]},{"id":"jehiel_770","name":"Jehiel","also":"","summary":"One of the Levites “of the second degree,” appointed to conduct the music on the occasion of the ark’s being removed to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]},{"id":"shemiramoth_2651","name":"Shemiramoth","also":"","summary":"A Levite in David’s time (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]},{"id":"elipheleh_1146","name":"Elipheleh","also":"","summary":"God will distinguish him, one of the porters appointed to play “on the Sheminith” on the occasion of the bringing up of the ark to the city of David (1 Chr. 15:18, 21).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,21]},{"id":"jaaziel_672","name":"Jaaziel","also":"Aziel","summary":"Comforted by God, a Levitical musician (1 Chr. 15:18).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]},{"id":"maaseiah_1849","name":"Maaseiah","also":"","summary":"One of the Levites whom David appointed as porter for the ark (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]},{"id":"mikneiah_2080","name":"Mikneiah","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,21]},{"